{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service at 3a45e1f256185399852b20a3695833a93812b5b8 — the merge station's second source exposed over HTTP, plus the regenerated browser embed, under ratified proposal c26a7f57 (25981e55). internal/service/ui.go adds POST /v0/landed: it takes a bounded list of commits and answers, for each, whether the mainline already carries it. The trust boundary is the point of the shape. The browser names commits, never the ref; the service resolves the mainline itself, trying refs/heads/main then refs/heads/master, and returns the name it used so the page can say \"landed on main\" rather than inventing it. When no mainline resolves, every answer is unknown with that stated as the reason — not absent, because no branch to compare against is not evidence that nothing landed. Commit names are validated in the storage layer before any process starts, so a ref name arriving where a commit belongs is refused rather than resolved. Nothing is stored: the station asks at render time, because a field somebody types can be stale by hand and one was. This preserves the distinctions the layer owes — kernel refusal, application interpretation, durable state, live state — and adds ordinary Git history as a fourth, which docs/reference/architecture.md records at this same head. internal/service/uidist carries the regenerated two-screen browser build. Conditions actually met at this exact head: a new server test drives the endpoint against a real repository with a merged head and an unmerged side branch, asserting the response names the branch, returns one answer per commit in order, reports the merged head landed and the side head absent, and refuses the string \"main\" as a commit because only the server chooses the ref. go vet, go test -count=1 ./..., go test -race -count=1 ./..., and the docset gates all pass; make ui at this head leaves git status --porcelain empty, so the committed embed matches the CI-locked build byte-for-byte. Carried once onto main bbc81674; the intervening merges changed internal/app, docs/reference/performance.md, README.md and performance/ only, with no file overlap here. Predecessor at this exact path: 874150d7 (#6782) at 889a64a2, to be retired at merge.","body":{"commit":"3a45e1f256185399852b20a3695833a93812b5b8","path":"internal/service"}}